<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_OllathrixEgg.xml                WEBWORK_NEST_EGG_ECONOMY_1
  ============================================================================
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_owner_and_nest_2026-09-23.md §4a
  ("The item — RM_OllathrixEgg") plus the 2026-09-24 blackmarket sitting's own
  authoring constraints on this exact def
  (webwork_egg_blackmarket_2026-09-24.md line ~282): tradeTags carries
  RM_Contraband and tradeability is set EXPLICITLY (not left to the parent's
  default) so the campaign's later PatchOperationReplace on <tradeability> has
  a real node to match — a Replace on an absent element silently matches
  nothing (the trader-strip lesson, cited by that same sitting note).

  🔴 BAN, per §4a's own table: this must NOT hatch. No CompHatcher, no
  CompTemperatureRuinable hatch path — a hatching egg is a tamed Ollathrix by
  the back door (ban 1: no tamed, traded or negotiated Ollathrix). It is inert
  cargo, same posture as a mined resource, which is also why ParentName is
  ResourceBase (the same parent RUT_FungalSoil/RM_SeveredTentacleFlesh already
  use for a perishable raw organic good) and not any Egg/AnimalProductRaw
  parent that would carry hatching machinery.

  Numbers are INVENTED against the sitting's own ❓ ranges (350-500 silver,
  ~2kg): MarketValue 400, Mass 2. daysToRotStart 15 IS the ruled figure
  (§4a: "the eggs are perishable... 15 days"), not invented.

  No ingestible, no recipe consumes it (ban check, §4a) — ResourceBase and
  CompProperties_Rottable alone carry no such hooks by default.

  PLACEHOLDER ART: flat placeholder generated by
  art/Items/gen_ollathrix_egg_placeholder.py, same "never ship magenta"
  posture as OLLATHRIX_OWNER_SPECIES_1's own placeholder. Real art queued,
  infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/webwork_nest.csv (RM_OllathrixEgg_v1 row) —
  0 hits for "ollathrix"/"clutch"/"nestwall" in registry.jsonl at authoring
  time (6594 lines), sanity-probed against "webwork" (36 hits).
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_OllathrixEgg</defName>
    <label>ollathrix egg</label>
    <description>A leathery, bone-white egg the size of a bowling ball, still faintly warm from the clutch it was pulled out of, faintly dusted with silk. Nothing has ever hatched one away from the mother's own nest. Traders who deal in these are not buying livestock — they are buying a very particular, very illegal kind of cargo, and it does not keep for long.</description>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_OllathrixEgg/RM_OllathrixEgg</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <stackLimit>10</stackLimit>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>400</MarketValue>
      <Mass>2</Mass>
      <Flammability>0.6</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>2</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
    <!-- Free tier default: only a nest can ever produce one (sitting §4a).
         The campaign's black-market layer (WEBWORK_EGG_BLACKMARKET_BUILD_1)
         patches this to All so a Cartel trader kind can stock it; that patch
         is not built here and does not exist yet. -->
    <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>RM_Contraband</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Rottable">
        <daysToRotStart>15</daysToRotStart>
        <rotDestroys>true</rotDestroys>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
